# Player API Integration

## Purpose
Integration patterns for native Player API functionality in SND macros.

## Scope
This rule covers Player API access patterns, entity management, job information, status checking, and player state management.

## Complete Player API Reference

### Core Player Properties
```lua
-- Player availability and state
Player.Available -> boolean
Player.IsBusy -> boolean
Player.IsMoving -> boolean
Player.IsInDuty -> boolean
Player.IsOnIsland -> boolean
Player.IsLevelSynced -> boolean
Player.SyncedLevel -> number
Player.Revivable -> boolean
Player.CanMount -> boolean
Player.CanFly -> boolean
```

### Player Information
```lua
-- Grand Company information
Player.GrandCompany -> number
Player.GCRankMaelstrom -> number [rw]
Player.GCRankImmortalFlames -> number [rw]
Player.GCRankTwinAdders -> number [rw]

-- Fishing information
Player.FishingBait -> number
```

### Player Object Access
```lua
-- Core player objects
Player.Entity -> EntityWrapper
Player.FreeCompany -> FreeCompanyWrapper
Player.Job -> JobWrapper
Player.Gearset -> GearsetWrapper
Player.Gearsets -> table<GearsetWrapper>
Player.Status -> table<StatusWrapper>
Player.Bingo -> BingoWrapper
```

### Player Methods
```lua
-- Job and gearset access
Player.GetJob(number classJobId) -> JobWrapper
Player.GetGearset(number id) -> GearsetWrapper
```

## Basic Player API Integration

### Player Availability Check
```lua
-- Check if player is available
function IsPlayerAvailable()
    return Player.Available
end

-- Wait for player to be available
function WaitForPlayerAvailable(timeout)
    timeout = timeout or 30
    local startTime = os.clock()
    
    while not Player.Available and (os.clock() - startTime) < timeout do
        yield("/wait 0.1")
    end
    
    return Player.Available
end
```

### Player State Checking
```lua
-- Check if player is busy
function IsPlayerBusy()
    return Player.IsBusy or Player.IsMoving or Player.IsInDuty
end

-- Check if player can perform actions
function CanPlayerAct()
    return Player.Available and not Player.IsBusy and not Player.IsMoving
end

-- Check if player is in duty
function IsPlayerInDuty()
    return Player.IsInDuty
end

-- Check if player is on island sanctuary
function IsPlayerOnIsland()
    return Player.IsOnIsland
end
```

